❓Question
Given a string s, determine whether it is a palindrome after:
Converting uppercase letters to lowercase.
Removing all non-alphanumeric characters.
Return true if it is a palindrome, otherwise return false.

Example
Input:
"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama"
Output:
true

Explanation:
After removing spaces, punctuation and converting to lowercase:
"amanaplanacanalpanama"
This reads the same forward and backward.

✅Approach
Use replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9]", "") to remove non-alphanumeric characters.
Convert the resulting string to lowercase.
Use two pointers:
start → beginning
end → end
Compare characters at both pointers.
If they are different, return false.
Otherwise move both pointers toward the center.
If all characters match, return true.

Code
class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(String s) {
        String checkPalindrome = s.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9]", "").toLowerCase();
        int start = 0;
        int end = checkPalindrome.length() - 1;
        while(start < end) {
            if(checkPalindrome.charAt(start) != checkPalindrome.charAt(end)) {
                return false;
            }
            start++;
            end--;
        }
        return true;
    }
}

Time Complexity
O(n)
Space Complexity
O(n)
